chab is the command-line interface for Chab. It talks to Chab's public
REST API (/v1) using a scoped team API token from browser device login,
manual entry, or CHAB_API_KEY. Browser-issued guest trial credentials can be
used for the backend-advertised free operations without signup.

Quick start:
  chab version --json    # print build metadata for scripts
  chab setup             # set up and verify a copied team or guest key
  chab login             # authorize or replace a stored team API key
  chab whoami --json     # print authenticated team and token data
  chab doctor            # check local setup and API readiness
  chab profile list      # inspect local connection profiles
  chab config path       # print the local config and auth paths
  chab health            # inspect public API health
  chab errors --json     # inspect public API error catalog
  chab search web --help # start a recoverable operation
  chab files list        # inspect stored files
  chab operations schema search.web # inspect embedded operation schema
  chab api get /me --json # call a public API path directly
  chab mcp serve --help  # configure local MCP tools

Usage:
  chab [flags]
  chab [command]

Authentication and Identity
  auth        Inspect and manage API authentication
  login       Authorize and store an API or guest trial key
  logout      Remove the stored credential for the active profile
  setup       Set up a verified API or guest trial profile
  whoami      Show the authenticated team or guest principal

Management
  billing     Manage billing settings
  credits     Inspect team credits
  project     Manage projects
  tokens      Manage team API tokens
  usage       Show team API usage
  webhooks    Manage webhook endpoints and replays

Profiles and Configuration
  config      Inspect and edit non-secret CLI configuration
  profile     Manage connection profiles

Raw API Access
  api         Call public API endpoints directly

Operations
  business    Run business-data operations
  contacts    Run contact discovery operations
  convert     Run conversion operations
  examples    Run example operations
  llm         Run model operations
  operations  Inspect and recover Chab operations
  research    Run research operations
  scrape      Run scrape operations
  screenshots Run screenshot operations
  search      Run search operations
  seo         Run SEO operations
  translate   Run translation operations

Files and Connected Data
  drive       Work with connected drive files
  files       Work with stored files
  mail        Work with connected mail

Diagnostics and Utilities
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  doctor      Check local setup and API readiness
  errors      List public API error codes
  health      Show public API health
  help        Help about any command
  mcp         Run local MCP integrations
  version     Print build metadata

Flags:
      --api-base-url string   API base URL (Chab default uses www.chab.ai/v1; custom base URLs use <base-url>/v1)
      --auth-file string      path to the CLI auth file
      --base-url string       product web base URL
      --config string         path to the CLI config file
      --debug                 write redacted request details to stderr
  -h, --help                  help for chab
      --include-meta          include safe response metadata in machine output where supported
      --jq string             filter supported JSON output with a jq expression
      --json                  print stable JSON output where supported
      --locale string         response language sent as Accept-Language (en or de)
      --no-ansi               disable ANSI terminal controls and paging where supported
      --no-color              disable color in human output where supported
      --no-pager              disable pager use for long human output where supported
      --no-prompt             fail instead of prompting for interactive input
      --plain                 print copy-safe plain output where supported
      --profile string        profile to use for this invocation
      --template string       render supported JSON output with a Go text/template
      --yes                   accept supported confirmations for risky or destructive operations; does not supply missing input

Use "chab [command] --help" for more information about a command.
